{% extends "shell.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}{{ copy.unavailable_title }} · {{ copy.product }}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
{#
  One branch, deliberately. `RCA-002` FR-050 collapses expired, deleted, deletion-requested,
  session-unavailable, and actor-not-a-member into one indistinguishable surface, so this template
  takes no state, reads no query parameter, and has nothing to branch on. The beta journey's
  `expired.html.j2` branches on `?deletion=requested`; copying that here would reintroduce exactly
  the disclosure this surface exists to prevent.
#}
<section class="document-card" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <h1 id="page-title">{{ copy.unavailable_title }}</h1>
  <p class="lede">{{ copy.unavailable_intro }}</p>
  {#
    The way out, and the same one the journey's `expired` offers: identical string, identical target,
    always present. `FR-050` collapses five causes into this surface and forbids telling them apart
    by navigation state, so an exit that varied -- in wording, in destination, or in whether it
    appears at all -- would reintroduce the disclosure the surface exists to prevent. It names no
    cause, which is `FR-052` holding too.

    `/app/{language}` rather than an organization-scoped address: this surface is reached with no
    resolved organization, and the chooser re-resolves scope from the session.
  #}
  <p><a href="{{ prefix }}/{{ language }}">{{ copy.recovery_exit }}</a></p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
